{"name":"Frolic","hex":"#f9e7e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frolic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Merry, joyous, full of mirth; later especially, frolicsome, sportive, full of playful mischief. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Free; liberal; bountiful; generous."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make merry; to have fun; to  romp; to behave playfully and uninhibitedly.","To cause to be merry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frolic"}],"entries":[{"title":"HMS Frolic","blocks":[{"text":"Five vessels of the British Royal Navy have been named HMS Frolic."},{"items":["The first HMS Frolic (1806) was an 18-gun 384 ton brig-sloop in service from 1806 to 1813. See also Capture of HMS Frolic.","The second HMS Frolic (1820) was a 10-gun 236 ton brig-sloop launched in 1820 and sold 1838.","The third HMS Frolic (1842) was a 16-gun 511 ton sloop launched in 1842 and sold 1864.","The fourth HMS Frolic (1872) was a composite screw gunboat launched in 1872. Converted to a drillship in 1888. Renamed WV.30 on conversion to a Coastguard watchvessel in 1893 and renamed WV.41 in 1897. Sold in April 1908.","The fifth HMS Frolic (1943) was a Lend-Lease Auk-class minesweeper launched in 1943, returned to the United States Navy in 1947, and in turn sold to the Turkish Navy as a survey ship, serving as TCG Çandarlı until 1986."]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HMS_Frolic","wikidata":"Q1259033"},{"title":"USS Frolic","blocks":[{"text":"USS Frolic is a name used more than once by the United States Navy, and may refer to:"},{"items":["USS Frolic (1813), a sloop of war in active service during 1814 until captured by the British during the War of 1812","USS Frolic, a side wheel steamer in commission as USS Advance from 1864 to 1865 and as USS Frolic from 1865 to 1869, from 1869 to 1870, from 1872 to 1874, and from 1875 to 1877","USS Frolic (1892), a patrol yacht in commission in 1898, from 1900 to 1906, and from 1906 to 1907","USS Frolic (SP-1336), a schooner in non-commissioned service from 1917 to 1918"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Frolic","wikidata":"Q7869512"},{"title":"Frolic (instrumental)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Frolic\" is an instrumental by the Italian composer Luciano Michelini. It was composed in 1974 for the film La bellissima estate, where it was used to represent the character of the barone rosso. \"Frolic\" is better known as the theme from the American sitcom Curb Your Enthusiasm. It was chosen by the series' creator, Larry David, who had heard the music in a bank advertisement four years prior. Apart from that, \"Frolic\" has been used as backing music for several advertisements, and in a rap song by Snoop Dogg."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frolic_(instrumental)","wikidata":"Q118945325"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Larry_David_at_the_2009_Tribeca_Film_Festival_2.jpg/500px-Larry_David_at_the_2009_Tribeca_Film_Festival_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Larry_David_at_the_2009_Tribeca_Film_Festival_2.jpg/1280px-Larry_David_at_the_2009_Tribeca_Film_Festival_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Larry_David_at_the_2009_Tribeca_Film_Festival_2.jpg/500px-Larry_David_at_the_2009_Tribeca_Film_Festival_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Larry David decided to use \"Frolic\" as the theme for Curb Your Enthusiasm after hearing it in a bank advertisement.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarry_David_at_the_2009_Tribeca_Film_Festival_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Directed_by_Robert_B._Weide.jpg/500px-Directed_by_Robert_B._Weide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par